<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>ContainEye: Server &amp; Docker checks from your phone</title>
    <meta name="description" content="ContainEye is an iPhone &amp; iPad app for working with your servers: SSH terminal, SFTP files, live monitoring, Docker &amp; Compose controls, automated tests, and an assistant.">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/retro.css">
</head>

<body>
    <div id="site-nav"></div>

    <main class="page">
        <section class="hero" id="hero">
            <p class="sub-header">ContainEye</p>
            <h1>Your servers, in your <em>pocket</em>.</h1>
            <p class="lead">Server and Docker checks from your phone.</p>

            <div class="term" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="term-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>containeye, ssh</span></div>
                <div class="term-body" id="term-body"><span class="cursor"></span></div>
            </div>

            <div class="checks" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="check"><i></i>web-01 · healthy</span>
                <span class="check"><i></i>db-01 · healthy</span>
                <span class="check"><i></i>4 tests passing</span>
                <span class="check"><i></i>12 containers running</span>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section>
            <div class="reveal container-wrapper">
                <div class="subnav">
                    <a href="/containeye/index" class="subnav-link active">Overview</a>
                    <a href="/containeye/features" class="subnav-link">Features</a>
                    <a href="/containeye/ssh-terminal" class="subnav-link">SSH Terminal</a>
                    <a href="/containeye/servers-management" class="subnav-link">Servers</a>
                    <a href="/containeye/automated-tests" class="subnav-link">Tests</a>
                    <a href="/containeye/faq" class="subnav-link">FAQ</a>
                    <a href="/containeye/support" class="subnav-link">Support</a>
                </div>

                <div class="doc-content">
                    <h2>What you can do</h2>
                    <p>ContainEye helps with day-to-day server tasks: connect quickly, run commands, browse files, watch your servers, and keep repeatable checks visible. It's organised into five tabs: <strong>SFTP</strong>, <strong>Terminal</strong>, <strong>Servers</strong>, <strong>Code</strong> (tests and snippets), and <strong>Agentic</strong> (an assistant).</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Full SSH terminal with a multi-tab workspace, themes, and command suggestions.</li>
                        <li>SFTP file browser with upload, download, rename, and a built-in text editor.</li>
                        <li>Live server monitoring: CPU, memory, disk, network, and processes.</li>
                        <li>Docker and Docker Compose controls: start, stop, restart, pull images.</li>
                        <li>Automated tests, from 13 built-in suggestions or drafted by the assistant.</li>
                        <li>Agentic assistant that operates your servers through approved commands.</li>
                        <li>Shortcuts actions and a home-screen widget for your tests.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <div class="cta-buttons">
                        <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/containeye-terminal-docker/id6741063706" class="nav-link">Get it on App Store</a>
                        <a href="/containeye/features" class="nav-link">Open feature docs</a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>

    <script src="/js/components.js"></script>
    <script>
        (function () {
            var body = document.getElementById('term-body');
            if (!body) { return; }
            var reduced = window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

            var script = [
                { t: '$ ', cls: 'prompt', instant: true },
                { t: 'ssh deploy@web-01', cls: '' },
                { t: '\n✓ connected in 0.4s', cls: 'ok', pause: 350 },
                { t: '\n$ ', cls: 'prompt', instant: true, pause: 250 },
                { t: 'docker ps --format "{{.Names}}: {{.Status}}"', cls: '' },
                { t: '\napi: Up 6 days', cls: 'dim', pause: 300 },
                { t: '\npostgres: Up 6 days (healthy)', cls: 'dim' },
                { t: '\ncaddy: Up 6 days', cls: 'dim' },
                { t: '\n✓ all tests passing', cls: 'ok', pause: 400 },
                { t: '\n$ ', cls: 'prompt', instant: true }
            ];

            var cursor = body.querySelector('.cursor');

            function write(text, cls) {
                var span = document.createElement('span');
                span.className = 'line ' + (cls || '');
                span.textContent = text;
                body.insertBefore(span, cursor);
            }

            if (reduced) {
                script.forEach(function (s) { write(s.t, s.cls); });
                return;
            }

            var si = 0;
            function nextStep() {
                if (si >= script.length) { return; }
                var step = script[si++];
                if (step.instant) {
                    write(step.t, step.cls);
                    setTimeout(nextStep, step.pause || 60);
                    return;
                }
                var ci = 0;
                var span = document.createElement('span');
                span.className = 'line ' + (step.cls || '');
                body.insertBefore(span, cursor);
                (function type() {
                    if (ci < step.t.length) {
                        span.textContent += step.t.charAt(ci++);
                        setTimeout(type, span.textContent.charAt(ci - 1) === '\n' ? 120 : 14 + Math.random() * 26);
                    } else {
                        setTimeout(nextStep, step.pause || 120);
                    }
                })();
            }
            setTimeout(nextStep, 700);
        })();
    </script>
</body>

</html>
